Weekly email number 4 =F0=9F=91=BE (Half way through the MTC)

Highlight of the week was either getting to drink like 6 glasses of milk a
day =F0=9F=90=84 or getting to build a cardboard air redirection system =E2=
=98=A2=EF=B8=8F (both of
which I have pictures of (although one is a picture of me after having
drank all of the cafeteria milk))

This week has been great all-round. Language immersion and classes have
been really exhausting but I'm mostly just happy to have the practice for
when i'm out in the field. It's questionable whether everyone else agrees
with 7 hours of classes a day, but they will definitely not complain when
they're teaching in Japan =F0=9F=98=82

Last week I mentioned how the hardest part about my mission was having my
companion, and while it still probably is most of the time, things have
gotten better as I seek to serve and share valuable time with him.
Definitely going better on that front.

This week I've been loving what I've read from Alma, I never knew just how
neat of a story it was reading about Alma and Amulek, they went through a
lot together. One of our instructors also shared about it during our
companion interview thing and said that things would go well if we
strengthen each other. I think that as I am more open and friendly with my
companion we'll be better able to achieve that. :^)

Our district has also grown a lot together over the past little while,
probably because we are all working hard together with such a difficult
language. Speaking of which, my Japanese is slowly but surely coming along.
It's definitely not easy, but I'm finding I am more able to get across my
general intentions which is a big win. =E2=9C=8C=EF=B8=8F

Food this week was probably just average (maybe made worse by the fact that
the lines take upwards of 40 minutes for a single plate) but I have
genuinely been drinking 4-6 glasses of milk a day, and that makes me very
happy =F0=9F=98=81

I am also proud to report that I have made no shortage of jokes throughout
each day, and I sincerely hope that it makes things a little more =F0=9F=A7=
=B8able
for those around me. (Not sorry)
I think I'd probably explode if I didn't share my energy with those around
me. I'm physically tired by the end of each day but I haven't yet felt like
it has been a drag, which I'm a bit surprised about to be honest.

Well, that's most of my allotted time for now, but I love yall, and I am
thinking about yall :)
=E3=81=98=E3=82=83=E3=81=82=E3=81=AD=F0=9F=91=8B

Scripture of the week
(From Alma 17)
11 And the Lord said unto them also: Go forth among the Lamanites, thy
brethren, and establish my word; yet ye shall be patient in long-suffering
and afflictions, that ye may show forth good examples unto them in me, and
I will make an instrument of thee in my hands unto the salvation of many
souls.

I Feel like this is pretty relevant to me especially as we're sometimes
having a tough time in the MTC (will probably not get easier once we get to
Japan lol) But as we are willing to sometimes go against the norm, we will
be strengthened in our trials =F0=9F=92=AA
In the name of Jesus Christ, Amen.

Bye for real :)

--000000000000b222d0061f609c48
